Actually, I've already thought about doing something like that. To avoid  
giving too much information to unspoiled players, the idea would be to set  
up proper flags not at entrance to the level but sometime later.
Typically, the "stair to Minetown/Soko" info should only be displayed once  
the player actually took a step in the Mines/Soko. Since the name of the  
dungeon branch is usually displayed on the status line, this will not give  
extra information to an unspoiled player.
For special levels, the flag should be set when the special feature is  
seen. Typically once the Oracle/Medusa/demon prince is in sight. Of  
course, this might cause some trouble with demon summoning (if the prince  
is killed before you enter his level)...
Minetown/end is also a minor problem. The specific feature of minetown may  
be the altar (usually, once you've seen it you've already seen several  
shops and guessed that this is a special level). For Minesend, it's  
usually the luckstone but that would give too much information to an  
unspoiled player... Plus saying that this is really the last level of  
mines and he should not search for stairs (at least in vanilla) is also a  
bit spoily...

Of course, this will require much more extra coding...

